<TopicLayout slug="joy">
  <p class="interlude">Joy: A feeling of great pleasure and happiness.</p>
  <p class="lede">
  </p>
  "Agreement with God is the seed of perfect holiness and perfect happiness."
  <br> - Charles Spurgeon
  <ul>
    <li>
      ...do not grieve, for the joy of the Lord is your strength. - Nehemiah 8:10
      <span class="meditation">Meditation: The Joy of God is so important because without it we are weak.
        <br> Find strength for today by seeking the joy that is only found in Jesus.</span>
    </li>
    "Philosophers," said the wise man, "can dance without music." and true believers in God can rejoice when outward comforts fail them.
    <br>May God grant us grace, then, to rejoice in our deepest distress, because the Lord is our sure possession, our perpetual heritage of joy."
    <br>- Charles Spurgeon
    <li>
      “As the Father has loved me, so have I loved you. Now remain in my love. If you keep my commands, you will remain in my love, just as I have kept my Father’s commands and remain in his love. I have told you this so that my joy may be in you and that your joy may be <b>complete</b>." 
      <br>- Jesus (John 15:9-11)
      <span class="meditation">Meditation: God wants our joy to be complete, and our joy becomes complete by remaining in His love. 
        <br>And there is no true remaining or flourishing in His love when we turn a def ear to His commands.
        <br>So pay attention to the Bible, God's love letter to us, and experience the true joy to be had!
      </span>
    </li>
    <li>
      "So with you: Now is your time of grief, but I will see you again and you will rejoice, and no one will
      take away your joy." 
      <br>- Jesus (John 16:22)
      <span class="meditation">Meditation: NO ONE, NOTHING, will be able to take away the joy a Christain has in seeing Christ again! 
        <br>"Let us acknowledge the Lord ; let us press on to acknowledge him. As surely as the sun rises, he will appear; he will come to us like the winter rains, like the spring rains that water the earth.” 
        <br> - Hosea 6:3
      </span>

    </li>
    <li>
      You make known to me the path of life; you will fill me with joy in your presence, with eternal
      pleasures at your right hand. - Psalms 16:11
      <span class="meditation">Meditation: Joy is found in the presence of Jesus</span>
    </li>
    "A Christian ought to be the most cheerful of men."
    <br> - CS Lewis
    <br>
    <br>
    "Be happy life isn't fair, if it were we would all be headed to a very hot place." (Hell)
    <br> - Wyne Riddering
    <br>
    <br>
    "To praise God is heaven. When immersed in adoration, we are completely filled with happiness, but to be totally devoid of gratitude is to be totally devoid of joy."
    <br> - Charles Spurgeon
  </ul>

